   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2020-06-08",
   "text": "Katherine's Lung Cancer Early Detection and Survival Act of 2020\n\n This bill requires private health insurance plans to cover, without cost sharing, screenings for the detection of lung cancer for individuals 40 years of age and older without regard to such individual's smoking history."
